DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These entry points manipulate various attributes of a file or directory,
     including file permissions, owner, group, size, access time and modifica‐
     tion time.

     VVOOPP__SSTTAATT() returns data in a format suitable for the stat(2) system call
     and by default is implemented as a wrapper around VVOOPP__GGEETTAATTTTRR().
     Filesystems may want to implement their own variant for performance rea‐
     sons.

     For VVOOPP__GGEETTAATTTTRR() and VVOOPP__SSEETTAATTTTRR() the arguments are:

     _v_p    The vnode of the file.

     _v_a_p   The attributes of the file.

     _c_r_e_d  The user credentials of the calling thread.

     For VVOOPP__SSTTAATT() the arguments are:

     _v_p           The vnode of the file.

     _s_b           The attributes of the file.

     _a_c_t_i_v_e___c_r_e_d  The user credentials of the calling thread.

     _f_i_l_e___c_r_e_d    The credentials installed on the file description pointing
                  to the vnode or NOCRED.

     Attributes which are not being modified by VVOOPP__SSEETTAATTTTRR() should be set to
     the value VNOVAL; VVAATTTTRR__NNUULLLL() may be used to clear all the values, and
     should generally be used to reset the contents of _*_v_a_p prior to setting
     specific values.

LLOOCCKKSS
     Both VVOOPP__GGEETTAATTTTRR() and VVOOPP__SSTTAATT() expect the vnode to be locked on entry
     and will leave the vnode locked on return.  The lock type can be either
     shared or exclusive.

     VVOOPP__SSEETTAATTTTRR() expects the vnode to be locked on entry and will leave the
     vnode locked on return.  The lock type must be exclusive.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     VVOOPP__GGEETTAATTTTRR() returns 0 if it was able to retrieve the attribute data via
     _*_v_a_p, otherwise an appropriate error is returned.  VVOOPP__SSEETTAATTTTRR() returns
     zero if the attributes were changed successfully, otherwise an appropri‐
     ate error is returned.  VVOOPP__SSTTAATT() returns 0 if it was able to retrieve
     the attribute data _*_s_b, otherwise an appropriate error is returned.

EERRRROORRSS
     [EPERM]            The file is immutable.

     [EACCES]           The caller does not have permission to modify the file
                        or directory attributes.

     [EROFS]            The file system is read-only.

